        {
          "id": "SP_CRIBELLOPORA_SIMPLEX_GAUTIER_1957",
          "name": "Cribellopora simplex Gautier, 1957",
          "rank": "SPECIES",
          "commonName": "",
          "lineage": "Cribellopora",
          "subspeciesCount": 0,
          "description": "Colony encrusting, unilaminar. Autozooids oval to subhexagonal, arranged in alternating series, and separated by distinct grooves. Frontal shield convex, heavily calcified, more prominent distally; uniformly perforated by complex pores; internally the pores are rounded, simple; externally they are subdivided into 2 – 5 (normally 3) rounded smaller pores by several radial partitions; frequently some small, slender denticles are produced from the edges of these sub-pores, without closing them. Primary orifice wide, semi-elliptical; proximal border straight, with a small, shallow U-shaped sinus occupying one third of the proximal border. Condyles rounded, beaded. Operculum chitinised, with a marginal horseshoe-shaped sclerite, more developed laterally. Peristomial region well developed, forming a flared, horseshoe-shaped peristome. Distal oral spines 1 – 3 distal, evanescent, their bases difficult to see, even by SEM. Large basal pore-chambers (dietellae) present. Ovicell globular, somewhat flattened frontally and hardly prominent, closed by the zooidal operculum; central area with an irregular umbo; a row of partitioned pseudopores placed in an arc on the distal slope of the ovicell. Maternal zooids with two stout lateral spines resting on the ovicell surface. Ancestrula tatiform, with 9 peripheral spines from the peripheral gymnocyst.",
          "sourcedFrom": "gbif",
          "wikipediaTitle": "gbif:4288395"
        },
