        {
          "id": "SP_ARTHROPOMA_CECILII",
          "name": "Arthropoma cecilii",
          "rank": "SPECIES",
          "commonName": "",
          "lineage": "Arthropoma",
          "subspeciesCount": 0,
          "description": "<p>Arthropoma cecilii is an encrusting bryozoan that forms extensive white or silvery patches varying in size and shape. The colony is composed of a single layer of autozooids. Autozooids are hexagonal to rectangular and longer than they are wide. </p>",
